    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Yordan Alvarez** (78.56) anchoring the lineup as the clear top-tier options. **Trea Turner** benefits from an elite matchup against Jackson Kent (5.54 xERA) and a favorable batting order position, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start despite a neutral park factor, purely due to his elite 0.443 xwOBA and platoon advantage against Michael Wacha. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.88) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) also rate as strong plays; both are heavily elevated by favorable matchups against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez and Janson Junk, respectively, and their lead-off duties maximize their potential for stolen bases, a critical scarcity category for our roster build.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (51.91), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Carson Benge** (53.96). While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** carries a solid platoon edge against Sean Manaea, the optimizer favored **Carson Benge**\u2019s higher projected base efficiency and batting order context. **Pedro Ramirez** (54.27) also lingers in the marginal tier; while he benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, his historical #8 batting position creates a ceiling drag that keeps him as a secondary option today.\n\nRisks for today center on the reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for several of our key hitters, including **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Carson Benge**. Should any of these players move down in the order or be rested, their efficiency scores will require immediate recalibration. Furthermore, while we are targeting favorable xERA matchups, any deviation in the pitching plans of Fisher or Foster Griffin could dampen the expected output for **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, and **Chase Meidroth**. Monitor weather and late-scratch news closely as we approach first pitch.",
